---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Nav from '../components/Nav.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
---
<Base title="About" description="What Ops Underground is and why it exists.">
  <Nav />
  <article class="about">
    <header>
      <div class="eyebrow">About</div>
      <h1>What is this place?</h1>
    </header>
    <div class="body">
      <p>Ops Underground is a resource destination for GTM Engineers and Revenue Operators — the people who are being asked to build the systems, not just run them.</p>
      <p>The thesis here is simple: most of what passes for GTM stack advice is just better duct tape. More tools, more integrations, more workarounds. Nobody is telling you to think differently about the underlying problem.</p>
      <p>Every workaround you've built is live documentation of a gap your stack can't fill. The tools aren't the problem. The architecture is.</p>
      <p>Ops Underground exists to change that conversation — with architectural thinking, honest reporting from the field, and a point of view that respects your intelligence.</p>
      <hr />
      <p>This property is run by <a href="https://timgosnell.com">Tim Gosnell</a>, founder of <a href="https://commonthreadai.com">CommonThread AI</a>. The thinking here is informed by building RIDL — a revenue intelligence platform built on the premise that your AI isn't broken, your context is.</p>
    </div>
  </article>
  <Footer />
</Base>

<style>
  .about { max-width: 640px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 4rem 2.5rem 6rem; }
  .eyebrow { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 11px; letter-spacing: 0.16em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--green); margin-bottom: 1rem; }
  h1 { font-family: var(--font-serif); font-size: 2.8rem; font-weight: 400; color: var(--white); margin: 0 0 3rem; letter-spacing: -0.02em; }
  .body { font-size: 17px; line-height: 1.75; color: rgba(240,237,230,0.8); }
  .body p { margin: 0 0 1.5rem; }
  .body a { color: var(--green); border-bottom: 0.5px solid rgba(59,140,74,0.4); }
  .body a:hover { border-color: var(--green); }
  .body hr { border: none; border-top: 0.5px solid var(--border); margin: 2.5rem 0; }
</style>
